A runtime error in an $INCLUDE file names the line inside that file (_INCLERRORLINE, _INCLERRORFILE$, the unhandled-error message), also in module code after the SUBs that the compiler moves in front of the first SUB; _ERRORLINE stays the main-file line of the $INCLUDE. The legacy QIR had no include position, so _INCLERRORLINE was always 0. QB64 rejects labels between SUB/FUNCTIONs; expected output written by hand from QBasic/QB64 semantics.
